"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(log(n)) complexity by time and O(log(n)) by space.

It took a lot of effort to code this elegantly—without manually writing out every power of 10 up to the 15th.
The key clever trick is that, for each multiplier, we add numbers to the count again.
In other words, we don't say, "these numbers have one decimal place, and those have two." 
Instead, we say: each number is counted as many times as the number of thresholds it has crossed. 
Double-counting here isn't an error; 
it’s the whole point - it is precisely how we count the decimal places.
"""

class Solution:
    def countCommas(self, n: int) -> int:
        total = 0
        threshold = 1000
        while threshold <= n:
            total += n - threshold + 1
            threshold *= 1000
        return total
